<title>INDIA: Yield on Indian 91-day t-bill drops to 6.94 pct.</title>
<headline>Yield on Indian 91-day t-bill drops to 6.94 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Friday it set a cut-off price of 98.30 rupees at the five billion rupee weekly auction of 91-day treasury bills, against 97.84 at the previous auction.</p>
<p>Dealers said the yield worked out to 6.94 percent, down from 8.86 percent at the previous auction.  </p>
